  "problem": "Let $N$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $p(x)\\in N,$ where $p(x)={x}^{3}-1.$\n\nII. For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in N.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under addition.",
